<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dissolution of the Holy Roman Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1806</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The dissolution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> took place in 1806, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Emperor Francis II</a> abdicated the imperial title following <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s victories and the creation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a>. It brought an end to an institution that had existed for about a thousand years and opened the way to the reorganisation of the German lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dissolution-of-the-holy-roman-empire.jpg" alt="Dissolution of the Holy Roman Empire" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alphathon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Holy_Roman_Empire_1789.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
